    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/office-and-billing-manager-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Office and Billing Manager (Admin II)",
      "description": "Office and Billing Manager (Admin II) - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Office and Billing Manager (Admin II) 492551 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Responsible for the upkeep of fiscal matters including insurance billing, student records and supply budget. Serve as HIPAA Privacy and Security Officer for MAP. Assist with the maintenance of MAP policies and procedures. Provide support to the program director and associate director. Duties: - Work directly with MAP contracted billing agencies including the MC Accounting Office and any outside contractors for monthly MAP client billing. - Keep track of all client treatment plan authorizations and ensure concurrent authorizations are submitted accurately and by due date. - Ensure all new staff and students have completed necessary paperwork and agreements before beginning work and are added to necessary portals (i.e. data collection, etc). - Onboard new BCBA staff by working to get them credentialed with insurance providers. - Complete session note checks for all clients in data collection software to ensure that session notes and times match before billing for these services. - Run monthly Dropbox and Motivity security checks. - Actively seek out and remain up to date on monthly changes to insurance company policies, billing and authorizations. - Update families promptly with regard to insurance benefits and how those benefits are applied to billing. - Collect and document all coinsurance, copayments, and tuition payments, as well as scholarship awards, and apply to each client’s account. - Provide monthly bills to families and follow up to ensure payments are made and recorded. - Serve as HIPAA Privacy and Security Officer for MAP a. Responsibilities as the HIPAA Security Officer for MAP, with the following job duties: i. Overseeing the MAP HIPAA Security Compliance Program & policies and procedures ii. Providing periodic security reminders for MAP staff iii. Being a point of contact for HIPAA Security questions or complaints iv. Liaison with the Meredith IT Department related to compliance of HIPAA Security technical safeguards operated by IT v. Ensuring periodic evaluations of the HIPAA Security compliance program vi. Ensuring periodic PHI risk analysis and a corresponding risk management program b. Responsibilities as the HIPAA Privacy Officer for MAP, with the following job duties: i. Overseeing the MAP HIPAA Privacy Compliance Program & policies and procedures ii. Acting as a point of contact for HIPAA Privacy questions or complaints iii. Ensuring HIPAA Privacy compliance for MAP forms related to uses and disclosures of protected health information iv. Investigating parent or client HIPAA privacy complaints v. Reporting any PHI breaches as required by the HIPAA breach notification requirements - Continuously update training to ensure knowledge of HIPAA regulations. - Prioritize, maintain, and oversee MAP paperwork and policies for client confidentiality and HIPAA regulations to ensure that MAP remains in compliance. - Routinely update and maintain/document MAP paperwork and policies to support renewal of MAP’s DHHS license and ensure compliance with all DHHS regulations. - Work with Program Director and Associate Director in overseeing and maintaining Facility and Supply budgets. - Assist Program Director and Associate Director in tracking and acknowledging gifts received by the program. - Complete monthly credit card billing statements accurately and in a timely manner. - Run occasional errands, maintain supplies, and otherwise maintain a functional and efficient office. - Ensure proper maintenance of all client records. - Responsible for submitting and following up on facility work order requests - Submit for renewal of DHHS license each year - Opens and/or Closes facility as scheduled. - Ensure proper documentation of student and client incident reports - Work with the Program Director and Associate Director to prioritize other duties as assigned. Qualifications: EITHER - High school diploma and a minimum of three years experience in a similar position. Experience in educational setting is preferred. OR - Bachelor’s degree and a minimum of 1 year of experience Requirements: - Demonstrated competency in the field of online medical/mental/behavioral health insurance billing and coding. - At least one year of billing experience using electronic systems for an organization. - Demonstrated competency in all basic user software systems such as Word, Excel, Google Docs and Publisher - Demonstrated knowledge of HIPAA rules and regulations - Have at least one year experience working with an agency conducting in-network insurance billing - Have no substantiated finding of abuse or neglect listed on the North Carolina Health Care Personnel Registry. Preferred Qualifications: - Experience working with in-network billing for a behavioral healthcare provider in the state of North Carolina. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) f3b6fd23 Last Name (required) 40b691d8 Email (required) a2bb734c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 94987796 Last Name (required) b2b8d825 Email (required) bd91cadb Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/police-officer-part-time-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Police Officer, Part-time",
      "description": "Police Officer, Part-time - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Police Officer, Part-time 492552 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Part-time Closing at: Oct 27 2026 - 11:55pm EDT Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Provides comprehensive law enforcement, safety, and security services on a part-time basis to students, faculty, staff, and visitors through the efficient use of departmental resources. Enforces applicable federal laws, North Carolina General Statutes, and Meredith College policies. This position is classified as essential personnel under College policy and is subject to requirements regarding essential personnel. Performs essential police duties during inclement weather, emergency situations, or as campus needs dictate. This role also supports a developing campus police department by contributing to the continuous improvement of operations, procedures, and service delivery, while helping to foster a culture of professionalism, accountability, and community engagement. This position is for 2nd, 3rd and weekend shifts. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: - Responds to all calls for service and requests for assistance from Meredith College students, faculty, staff, and visitors - Exercises independent judgment to determine appropriate actions to resolve incidents, including detention, search, arrest, issuance of citations, and criminal charge filing in accordance with North Carolina law - Applies only the minimum level of force necessary, consistent with training, law, and departmental policy - Patrols campus by vehicle and on foot; operates a law enforcement patrol vehicle during day and night shifts - Controls access to campus facilities and designated areas, including the Greenway, during established hours - Responds to calls, fire alarms, and intrusion alarms, including suspicious persons, and takes appropriate enforcement or protective action - Conducts preliminary and follow-up investigations by interviewing victims, witnesses, suspects, and confidential informants; collects, preserves, and documents physical and digital evidence - Prepares detailed written reports, case files, and documentation in accordance with departmental policy and legal standards - Provides testimony in criminal, traffic, and judicial proceedings as required - Provides traffic, parking, and crowd control for campus events and special functions - Conducts safety and security inspections of campus facilities, including checking doors, windows, and lighting - Renders emergency and non-emergency medical assistance, including First Aid, CPR, and AED use, until relieved by medical professionals - Participates in community-oriented policing, crime prevention initiatives, campus outreach, and educational programming - Builds positive relationships with students, faculty, and staff through visibility, engagement, and service - May perform administrative duties such as campus bank deposits or other assignments as directed - Performs duties related to emergency response, disaster operations, and inclement weather safety responsibilities - Participates in the development and refinement of departmental practices, procedures, and service delivery models - Provides feedback to supervisors to support the growth and continuous improvement of a developing department Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: - Knowledge of federal laws, North Carolina General Statutes, and College policies applicable to sworn law enforcement officers - Ability to analyze complex situations, exercise sound judgment, and use discretion when dealing with difficult or hostile individuals - Ability to observe and recall names, faces, and details; maintain accurate notes and reports - Skill in operating law enforcement equipment, including radios, vehicles, and defensive tools - Ability to communicate clearly and professionally with diverse populations - Ability to understand and work within the scope of authority while applying policies and procedures consistently - Ability to adapt to evolving policies, procedures, and operational needs in a developing department - Commitment to maintaining the highest standards of integrity, professionalism, and ethical conduct Education & Experience: - High School Diploma or equivalent required - Current North Carolina Driver License with a clear driving history - Current certification as a sworn Law Enforcement Officer by the State of North Carolina (BLET) Training & Certification Requirements: - Successful completion of required annual in-service training and annual firearms qualification - Compliance with North Carolina Criminal Justice Education and Training Standards Commission requirements - Certification in or ability to obtain certification in First Aid, CPR, AED, ASP Baton, chemical agents, and other department-approved law enforcement tools and techniques - Successful completion of a basic physical fitness assessment prior to appointment and/or during probationary period, consistent with departmental standards Working conditions & physical demands: - Ability to work assigned part-time shifts, including nights, weekends, holidays, and emergency call-back - Duties performed in office, vehicle, and outdoor environments; subject to varying weather conditions - May be required to remain on duty during inclement weather or emergencies when relief is unavailable - Medium work: ability to walk extended distances, stand for long periods, climb stairs, run as necessary, and lift up to 50 pounds - Ability to navigate physical obstacles and assist individuals experiencing medical or safety emergencies - Vision correctable to meet North Carolina law enforcement standards, including color vision requirements Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) f4acd9d8 Last Name (required) 4e45b595 Email (required) 3281ced2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 7c028985 Last Name (required) ba1494be Email (required) f57b7bcc Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-housekeeping-shift-supervisor-2nd-shift-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states-923a47b8-8768-4a82-b75e-f96704c8614d": {
      "title": "Assistant Housekeeping Shift Supervisor",
      "description": "Assistant Housekeeping Shift Supervisor - 2nd Shift - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Assistant Housekeeping Shift Supervisor - 2nd Shift 492550 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Assistant Housekeeping Shift Supervisor serves as the lead worker for an assigned shift and assists the Housekeeping Shift Supervisor with the daily coordination of housekeeping operations. This position provides work direction, training, quality inspections, and operational support while also performing custodial duties. The Assistant Shift Supervisor helps ensure assigned facilities are maintained in a clean, safe, sanitary, and welcoming condition and supports the supervisor in maintaining productivity, customer service, safety, and quality standards. This position is designated as Essential Personnel under College policy and is required to respond during inclement weather, emergency events, and other campus operational needs. Regular Work Schedule: 2nd Shift: Monday through Friday, 2:00 p.m.- 10:30pm. Weekend and overtime work may be required based on operational needs. Duties: Daily Operations - Assist with coordinating daily work assignments and building coverage. - Assign and prioritize routine and special project work. - Monitor completion of assigned work and adjust assignments as operational needs change. - Perform quality inspections of completed work. - Assist with event support and project scheduling. - Ensure custodial supplies and equipment are available and properly maintained. Leadership - Provide day-to-day direction and guidance to housekeeping staff. - Train new employees in cleaning procedures, equipment operation, and safety practices. - Demonstrate proper custodial methods and departmental standards. - Assist with onboarding new employees. - Promote teamwork and positive employee relations. - Communicate departmental expectations and operational updates. Custodial Support - Perform all duties of a Housekeeper II as operational needs require. - Assist with specialized floor care and project work. - Respond to customer requests and building concerns. Safety & Compliance - Monitor compliance with departmental procedures and safety regulations. - Report equipment issues and facility deficiencies. - Assist with incident documentation. - Support emergency response and inclement weather operations. Administrative Support - Assist the Shift Supervisor with attendance monitoring, supply inventories, work orders, and operational documentation. - Provide input regarding employee performance and training needs. - Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: - Thorough knowledge of custodial methods and cleaning standards. - Ability to lead and motivate employees. - Ability to organize work assignments and prioritize competing demands. - Ability to inspect work for quality. - Strong interpersonal and customer service skills. - Ability to resolve routine workplace issues. - Ability to follow verbal and written instructions. - Ability to communicate effectively and professionally both verbally and in writing. - Proficiency with custodial equipment and cleaning chemicals. Education & Experience: - Minimum of 1 year of progressively responsible custodial experience. - Supervisory or lead experience preferred. - Demonstrated leadership and organizational skills. - Experience in training or leading employees preferred. Working conditions & physical demands: - Works in moderate noise all around campus, indoor and outdoor. - Frequent standing, walking, bending, use of repetitive motions and operating cleaning equipment. - Often lifts 10-50 lbs objects. - May be required to work during periods of inclement weather. - May be required to work weekends. Apply Now! First Name (required) b43f0d81 Last Name (required) 04161075 Email (required) 82bcfe0e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 0d8d22c4 Last Name (required) b787764d Email (required) 8bbbb47c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/housekeeper-i-2nd-shift-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Housekeeper I",
      "description": "Housekeeper I - 2nd Shift - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Housekeeper I - 2nd Shift 492549 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Housekeeper I performs routine custodial services that maintain a clean, safe, sanitary, and welcoming campus environment. Under the direction of the Housekeeping Shift Supervisor, this position is responsible for cleaning residence halls, classrooms, offices, restrooms, public spaces, and other assigned facilities in accordance with established departmental standards. This position performs routine housekeeping duties while developing proficiency in custodial methods, equipment, and campus procedures. Employees are expected to work collaboratively with other housekeeping staff and contribute to maintaining a positive customer experience for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This position is designated as Essential Personnel under College policy and is required to respond during inclement weather, emergency events, and other campus operational needs. Regular Work Schedule: 2nd Shift: Monday through Friday, 2:00 p.m.- 10:30pm. Weekend and overtime work may be required based on operational needs. Duties: - Clean assigned residence halls, academic buildings, administrative offices, classrooms, restrooms, and public areas according to departmental standards. - Perform routine floor care, including sweeping, dust mopping, damp mopping, vacuuming, and spot cleaning. - Operate standard custodial equipment safely and effectively. - Dust furniture, fixtures, ledges, vents, walls, and other surfaces. - Clean mirrors, glass doors, interior windows, and other glass surfaces. - Clean and sanitize restrooms, including sinks, toilets, urinals, mirrors, partitions, and dispensers. - Empty trash and recycling containers and transport waste to designated collection areas. - Restock restroom supplies and other consumable custodial products. - Report maintenance issues, damaged equipment, safety concerns, or unusual building conditions to the supervisor. - Assist with project work, including deep cleaning, carpet care, furniture moving, and event setup or breakdown as assigned. - Participate in emergency response activities and facility recovery efforts as directed. - Duties may include inclement weather safety responsibilities, including the removal of snow, ice and/or branches, and other related responsibilities as necessary due to inclement weather. - May be required to work during campus closures. - Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities - Ability to learn and perform standard custodial procedures and practices. - Ability to safely operate custodial equipment and tools, including pressure washers when assigned. - Ability to follow written and verbal instructions. - Ability to communicate effectively and professionally with supervisors, coworkers, students, faculty, staff, and visitors. - Ability to work cooperatively as part of a team. - Ability to recognize and report maintenance or safety concerns. - Ability to maintain confidentiality while working in offices and other sensitive areas. Education & Experience: - Previous custodial, janitorial, hospitality or related experience in commercial, institutional, healthcare, hospitality, or higher education is preferred. - Ability to successfully learn departmental cleaning procedures, equipment operation, and safety practices. - Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented environment. Working conditions & physical demands: - Works in moderate noise all around campus, indoor and outdoor. - Frequent standing, walking, bending, use of repetitive motions and operating cleaning equipment. - Often lifts 10-50 lbs. objects. - May be required to work during periods of inclement weather. Apply Now! First Name (required) cc4d9fbf Last Name (required) 7edcb14e Email (required) a7f07410 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 4cd8f026 Last Name (required) 897287f6 Email (required) 1f3e5ef5 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
