    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-to-the-vice-president-for-marketing-and-communications-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant to the Vice President for Marketing and Communications",
      "description": "Assistant to the Vice President for Marketing and Communications - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Assistant to the Vice President for Marketing and Communications 492548 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The position serves as an executive partner to the Vice President of Marketing and Communications and performs high level administrative and project coordination tasks for a comprehensive, high volume Marketing and Communications Division. The position works with a high degree of confidentiality and requires discretion in handling sensitive conversations and documents, as well as maintaining strict confidentiality when supporting projects that involve executive leadership, trustees, prospective donors, high profile partners, or matters affecting the College’s brand and reputation. Duties: - Manages confidential information related to institutional strategy, personnel, budgets, contracts, external relations on behalf of the VPMC. - Actively manages the calendar and serves as a gatekeeper helping to ensure strategic focus for the VPMC. - Initiates, composes, reviews, and edits correspondence, presentations proposals, and announcements for the Vice President for Marketing and Communications. - Develops and maintains divisional databases, spreadsheets, project trackers, status reports, and other information-management tools to support executive priorities, monitor progress, and ensure timely follow-through. - Supports the Vice President for Marketing and Communications in planning, coordinating, and advancing strategic projects and initiatives, including tracking progress, coordinating stakeholders, and ensuring timely follow-through. - Supports divisional financial administration by maintaining budget records, monitoring designated budget lines, processing expense reports, and assisting with accounts payable and receivable. - Provides administrative and coordination support for divisional digital marketing operations, including website compliance and quality assurance, calendar entries, online marketing profiles, implementing intranet pages, and documentation and follow-up for web strategy meetings. - Provides administrative support for divisional revenue-generating activities, including scheduling, room reservations, facility tours, client documentation, event agreements, insurance, billing, and client tracking. - Occasionally supports the Campus Store in the absence of the Campus Store manager and/or during special events. - Assist with other projects and perform other duties as assigned by the Vice President of Marketing and Communications. Skills Needed: - Must be comfortable with Microsoft Office, including Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. - Must have strong interpersonal, customer service, written communication and proofreading skills. - Budget administration experience preferred. Key interfaces: - Works with staff from every campus division, including Executive Leadership Team offices, directors, administrative assistants, faculty, and committee representatives. Also interfaces with Board of Trustee members, external consultants, vendors, and members of the news media. Education & Experience: EITHER - High school diploma and a minimum of five years of experience in a similar position. Experience in educational setting is preferred. OR - Bachelor’s degree and at least three years of experience. - Some specialized training or experience may be required. Working conditions & physical demands: - General office setting with a moderate noise level. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 64933b03 Last Name (required) 9fbbb539 Email (required) da744fe0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 9bfc3645 Last Name (required) c1491bf5 Email (required) 7a30c839 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/clinical-educator-in-dietetics-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Educator in Dietetics",
      "description": "Clinical Educator in Dietetics - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Clinical Educator in Dietetics 492547 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Faculty Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Meredith College seeks qualified applicants for the position of Clinical Educator in Dietetics. This position is a full-time, eleven-month, instructor of professional practice, faculty appointment. Duties: - Eighteen to twenty-one credit hour teaching load of DI and MSN supervised experiential learning and/or didactic coursework. - Work both in designated hospital location(s) and on the Meredith College campus each week to educate students one-on-one or in small groups, both formally and informally. - Precept dietetic interns and graduate students on a rotating schedule in cohorts at one designated hospital location in Medical Nutrition Therapy/Clinical Nutrition. - Collaborate with the Program Director, hospital managers, and other community partners to plan and implement students’ schedules. - Fulfill all nutrition competencies as required by the hospital. - Model evidence-based practice, professional behavior, time management, and ethical practice. - Assist interns and students in setting appropriate goals and schedules for completing competencies during the rotation. - Identify and facilitate learning activities that support competencies/learning outcomes. - Evaluate each intern/student's progress and provide timely formative feedback to students on strengths and opportunities for growth regarding their provision of Medical Nutrition Therapy and overall professionalism. - Develop and lead campus-based clinical simulations and other alternate learning experiences in the Simulation Lab. - Complete required supervised practice documentation in a timely manner. - Collaborate regularly with the Program Director regarding student performance in supervised experiential learning sites, complete required documentation in a timely manner, and provide remediation when needed. - Assist in development of programmatic materials including preceptor education materials, supervised experiential learning list of required learning activities, rubrics, and authentic simulations, and marketing materials. - Collect and assess data to meet ACEND accreditation requirements. - Participate in the application review and selection process for program candidates. - Attend staff meetings at the hospital and college. - Perform other miscellaneous tasks within the graduate office as identified by the Program Director and/or Department Chair. Qualifications: - Master’s degree in Nutrition Science, Dietetics, or Public Health. Credentialed by CDR as an active Registered Dietitian. - At least three years of clinical nutrition experience is required. - The successful candidate will provide evidence of initiative, maturity, professionalism, attention to detail, excellent organizational ability, time management, and interpersonal skills, which include high-quality oral and written communication skills. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. To apply: submit your letter of interest, vita, teaching philosophy, copy of all transcripts, RD registration number, and list of references with contact information. Official transcripts are required upon hire. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume/CV - Teaching Philosophy - Copy of Transcripts - RD Registration Number - References (within the application) Apply Now! First Name (required) e240f134 Last Name (required) 85b81b20 Email (required) cfd0b6ae Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 59d348b3 Last Name (required) e6fcf313 Email (required) bc3e8a5a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/dietetics-educator-and-dietetic-internship-program-director-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Dietetics Educator and Dietetic Internship Program Director",
      "description": "Dietetics Educator and Dietetic Internship Program Director - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Dietetics Educator and Dietetic Internship Program Director 492546 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Faculty Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Meredith College seeks qualified applicants for the position of Dietetics Educator and Dietetic Internship Program Director. This position is a full-time, eleven-month, faculty appointment. Duties: Teaching responsibilities include on-campus undergraduate and graduate courses in Food and Nutrition. Expertise to teach a variety of food and nutrition courses at Undergraduate and Graduate levels. Serve as Program Director for ACEND accredited Dietetic Internship program and oversee supervised experiential learning. Active involvement within the department; student advising; DI program documentation and administration; scholarship and service to the profession expected. Qualifications: - Master’s degree in Nutrition Sciences, Dietetics, or Public Health. - RD credential with at least five years of professional experience required. - The successful candidate will provide evidence of initiative, maturity, professionalism, attention to detail, excellent organizational ability, time management and interpersonal skills, which include high-quality oral and written communication skills. - Demonstrated or potential excellence in undergraduate & graduate teaching. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. To apply: complete the online application, submit your letter of interest, vita, teaching philosophy, copy of all transcripts, RD registration number, and list of references with contact information. Official transcripts are required upon hire. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume/CV - Teaching Philosophy - Copy of Transcripts - RD Registration Number - References (within the application) Apply Now! First Name (required) c677d7dc Last Name (required) 71a5b8d7 Email (required) cf50aea3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) d0719f23 Last Name (required) d5e668b9 Email (required) a839e5a5 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
