    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/associate-director-of-admissions-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Associate Director of Admissions - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Associate Director of Admissions 492545 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Associate Director serves as a member of the admissions team that serves transfer, WINGS and graduate students. The Associate Director is responsible for assisting in the development and implementation of strategies to recruit, select, and enroll a diverse student body to meet college enrollment targets. The Associate Director will manage an assigned territory consisting of academic programs that serve adult and graduate populations. The Associate Director of Admissions should possess characteristics indicative of a strong collaborative leader: integrity, intellect, work ethic, initiative, creativity, flexibility, and enthusiasm for the work. Skills important for success in this position include excellent public speaking skills, strong writing skills, planning and problem-solving, interpreting data to inform and enhance recruitment strategies, and strong relationship-building and supervisory ability. Duties: - Meet enrollment goals for assigned academic area(s) by representing Meredith at community college visits, community events, working one-on-one with families during on-campus visits, while meeting or exceeding weekly outreach requirements for students across the admissions funnel - Serve as the primary liaison between admissions unit and department heads, faculty and Deans for assigned academic programs - Review applications and offer decisions on behalf of the college based on admissions criteria set by the program and/or college - Collaborate with the admission office leadership team to develop practices that enhance productivity and streamline application, admission, and enrollment processes - Responsibility for coordinating one or more recruiting events and assisting with other events as needed - Monitor and control costs of recruitment travel, and produce follow-up reports for the effectiveness of travel - Develop relationships with other college departments and key secondary school constituents to enhance customer service and satisfaction - Represent the Office of Admissions in a public-speaking capacity on and off campus and maintain records of these activities - Collaborate with campus constituents to develop and implement selected recruitment and pre-orientation events - Serve on College committees as assigned - Perform other related duties as needed or assigned Skills Needed: - Must have excellent interpersonal skills and be able to work with a diverse community - Ability to effectively communicate in person, via phone, and in writing and make effective public presentations - Strong relationship-building skills - Thorough understanding of College procedures, curricular offerings, student outcomes, and be able to relate this information effectively to prospective students and families - Must be able to understand and explain financial aid programs, eligibility criteria, and award procedures - Ability to interpret and apply data to decision-making - Ability to maintain an effective applicant tracking system - Strong planning and organization capabilities - Excellent time management and attention to detail Key interfaces: - Interacts with prospective students, families, and community college liaisons - Outreach and partnerships with local businesses and organizations - Office of Admission staff, and members of the Meredith community Education & Experience: - Master’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience required - Minimum of three - five years admissions and recruiting experience or related work - Valid NC Driver’s license required and clear driving history Working conditions & physical demands: - General office setting with moderate noise level - Frequent travel required - Evening and Weekend work required Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 925acc2a Last Name (required) c29499b6 Email (required) 01b6b568 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 5c362b43 Last Name (required) ae5beb9b Email (required) c9ff1f9e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/adjunct-faculty-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty 492541 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Adjunct Instructor Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Meredith college seeks qualified professionals for adjunct teaching positions for undergraduate and graduate courses in a variety of disciplines. Meredith College is a women’s institution for first-time traditional women college students, transfer students, adult degree completers, and both male and female graduate students. Built-in comprehensive coaching and advising are provided throughout the undergraduate experience to ensure students are supported and positioned for success. We are looking for adjunct faculty for the following disciplines: Business Administration (marketing, supply chain, data analytics, operations), Biology (anatomy and physiology, genetics), Chemistry, Computer Science, Criminal Justice, Data Analytics, History, Mathematics, Psychology, Political Science, Social Work, Statistics, French and Spanish. Qualifications: Education/Experience: - To be considered for a position in our applicant pool, applicants are required to possess a graduate (terminal) degree in the relevant field with a minimum of 18 graduate hours from an accredited university. - In addition to the graduate degree, expertise in teaching the subject matter is desired. - All graduate work must be documented with official transcripts submitted to the university upon request. - Teaching experience in traditional and/or online education is desired. - Experience working with either Brightspace or Canvas learning management systems is desired. Knowledge, Skills, And Abilities: - Communicate effectively to all groups through both oral and written channels. - Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Outlook, Excel, PowerPoint and the Internet. Application Instructions: Please include the following with your application: - Curriculum Vitae, required - Cover letter - Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts for all related degrees, licenses/certificates will be required upon hire) Optional Additional Attachments: - Teaching Philosophy - Sample Syllabus - Additional Licenses/Certifications - Course Evaluations Apply Now! First Name (required) af90a15a Last Name (required) 2b159ca4 Email (required) 42a9f213 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 4cd5f06b Last Name (required) 06c61000 Email (required) 73611d5d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/senior-programmer-analyst-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Programmer / Analyst",
      "description": "Senior Programmer / Analyst - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Senior Programmer / Analyst 492543 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. We are seeking an experienced Senior Ellucian Colleague Programmer Analyst to support, develop, and enhance our Ellucian Colleague ERP environment. The successful candidate will be responsible for designing, developing, implementing, and maintaining enterprise applications and integrations that support academic and administrative operations. This position works closely with functional departments and Information Systems staff to analyze business requirements, recommend technical solutions, and deliver high-quality applications that improve institutional efficiency. Essential Duties & Responsibilities: - Application Development: Design, develop, and document custom applications. - Testing & Quality Assurance: Perform unit testing, debugging, and code reviews to ensure high-quality, maintainable code. - Systems Integration: Create and support administrative software and interfaces (including Colleague, Ellucian Self-Service, ETHOS Integration, Informer, PowerFAIDS, CSGold, and Slate). - Reporting: Develop custom reports utilizing Informer and Colleague. - Upgrades & Deployment: Plan and implement Self-Service upgrades and custom application deployments. - Impact Analysis: Review Colleague software updates and determine their impact on custom modifications. - Project Collaboration: Lead or assist in projects, collaborate with users to develop testing procedures, and analyze impacts on other modules or applications. - Procedural Support: Support users in developing workflows and suggest procedural changes where necessary. - Security & Compliance: Ensure compliance with institutional security standards, data governance policies, and regulatory requirements. - Availability: Perform these and other duties during after-hours and weekends when occasionally required. Required Skills: - Leadership & Support: Must exemplify excellent customer support and leadership skills. - Communication: Strong verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work effectively with individuals of varying technical experience and knowledge. - Problem Solving: Strong logical, analytical, and problem-solving skills. - Collaboration: Proven ability to work productively both independently and within a team environment. - Organization: Excellent organizational skills with a strong, detail-oriented approach.= Education & Experience: - Education: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Management Information Systems, or a related field (or equivalent professional experience). - ERP Experience: 5+ years of experience developing and supporting Ellucian Colleague ERP applications. - Web Development: 2+ years of experience developing and deploying web applications using ASP.NET Core. - Methodologies: Strong knowledge of the software development life cycle (SDLC) and source code management using Git (or similar version control systems). - Technical Stack: Practical knowledge of Unidata/SQL, Unix, Unibasic, and Colleague Studio. - Compliance: Familiarity with data security standards, FERPA, and higher education compliance requirements. Working Conditions & Physical Demands: This position will initially require an on-site presence during the first 90 days of employment. Upon successful completion of the 90-day introductory period and demonstration of the ability to independently perform the essential duties of the position, the employee will be eligible to transition to a fully remote work arrangement, subject to organizational approval and applicable remote-work policies. Remote work must be completed within the state of North Carolina. Ability to work after hours and on weekends when urgent operational needs or maintenance windows require it. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 610a1047 Last Name (required) 93df6515 Email (required) 4285440d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) dff8c60e Last Name (required) 058c000e Email (required) 99b9ad11 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/security-officer-part-time-flexible-schedule-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Security Officer, Part-time (Flexible Schedule)",
      "description": "Security Officer, Part-time (Flexible Schedule) - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Security Officer, Part-time (Flexible Schedule) 492501 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Part-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Provides safety and security services to students, staff, faculty, and visitors through efficient use of departmental resources. Position is classified as essential personnel under college policy and is subject to college and department policies regarding essential personnel. Performs essential duties related to security work as identified by management during inclement weather, emergency situations, or as campus needs dictate. Position may require shift, weekend, and/or overtime work. Seeking applicants with maximum flexibility and the ability to be available on a call-in status. There are no guarantees on the number of hours per week. The position will fill in for vacation periods as well as work during holidays throughout the year. This position is less than 1,000 hours per year and is not eligible for benefits. First Shift hours: 7am – 3pm; Second Shift hours: 3pm – 11pm; Third Shift hours: 11pm – 7am. Duties : - Responds to all calls for service and request for assistance from Meredith College student, staff, faculty and visitors. - Determines necessary and appropriate actions needed to resolve problems and answers calls for service. May need to resort to applying minimum levels of force at times. - Patrols campus by vehicle or foot. Controls access to campus and the Greenway during closing hours. - Responds to any call, fire or intrusion alarms, including suspicious person(s) and take appropriate action. - Provides traffic direction for large and small events. - Enforces parking regulations, including towing and auto-booting as appropriate. Provides car unlock, jump start, and other automotive services to students, faculty, and staff. (Flat tires can be changed if the conditions are safe). - Checks doors and window of building to ensure they are secure. Turns on and turn off interior and exterior light according to set schedules or special request. - Duties may include inclement weather safety responsibilities as necessary due to inclement weather and activities related to emergency situations. - May be required to work during campus closures. - Assist in turning on and off campus lighting for Special Events and scheduled sports activities. Skills Needed: - Ability to use discretion in handling difficult persons and analyze situations likely to be encountered on patrol. - Observe and retain names, faces and details of occurrences; keep detailed notes for report writing and other daily log sheets, understand and correct emergency alarm systems. - Observe legal and defensive driving practices; interpret, apply and explain rules, regulations, policies and procedures. - Ability to understand and work within the scope of authority; apply policies and procedures. Key interfaces: - Responds to calls by students, faculty, staff and visitors. - May need to confront hostile or belligerent persons in an appropriate and professional manner. Education & Experience : - High School Diploma or equivalent required. - Current NC Driver License and clear driving history. - Previous security experience is a plus Working conditions & physical demands: - Position may require shift, weekend, and/or overtime work. Seeking applicants with maximum flexibility and the ability to be available on a call-in status.  There are no guarantees on the number of hours per week. The position will fill in for vacation periods as well as work during holidays throughout the year. This position is less than 1,000 hours per year and is not eligible for benefits. - Must be able to work any shift and respond/report for duty, as necessary. Part of duties may include general office setting with moderate noise level. Must be able to operate company vehicles. - Patrols campus outdoors and may be exposed to the weather. May be held for additional shifts during inclement weather, if relief is not possible. - Ability to navigate physical obstacles, such as walls, heights, etc. Ability to physically help students, faculty, and staff having health issues. - Must be able to walk for extended distances, stand for long periods, climb stairs, and run, as necessary. - Must occasionally lift up to 50 lbs. Apply Now! First Name (required) d089e987 Last Name (required) 453d3d47 Email (required) 11ef810a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) ab24a5d1 Last Name (required) 71bc42f3 Email (required) 1d08bd9c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/adjunct-instructor-of-genetics-and-or-human-anatomy-physiology-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Adjunct Instructor of Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology 492540 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Adjunct Instructor Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Biology Department at Meredith College invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to teach lecture and laboratory courses in Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology beginning Fall 2026. We seek colleagues committed to high quality undergraduate teaching, and supporting student success in a liberal arts environment. Responsibilities: - Teach lecture and/or laboratory sections in Genetics and/or Human Anatomy & Physiology - Develop and deliver course materials that align with departmental learning outcomes - Provide timely assessment, feedback, and academic support to students - Maintain clear communication with department leadership - Uphold all instructional, safety, and compliance standards for laboratory teaching Minimum Qualifications: - Master’s degree in Biology, Genetics, Physiology, or a closely related discipline - Demonstrated experience teaching undergraduate students or evidence of strong potential for effective instruction - Commitment to fostering a supportive learning environment Application Materials: • Cover letter describing teaching experience and areas of expertise • Curriculum vitae • Contact information for at least two professional references • (Optional) Sample syllabus or evidence of teaching effectiveness Appointment Details: Adjunct appointments are semester based and part time. Compensation is commensurate with qualifications and course load. Opportunities for continued teaching may be available based on departmental needs. How to Apply: Complete the online application. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until positions are filled. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume / CV - References (within the application) Apply Now! First Name (required) 01b37fb7 Last Name (required) 417f9e80 Email (required) fd05b562 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 2c458c6c Last Name (required) 0fae0a38 Email (required) 8e08837d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/director-of-career-planning-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Career Planning",
      "description": "Director of Career Planning - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Director of Career Planning 492529 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Director of Career Planning provides strategic leadership for a comprehensive, outcomes-driven career development program that supports students and alumnae in achieving meaningful post-graduate success. This role is responsible for aligning career services with the mission of the College and advancing institutional priorities related to student success, retention, and career outcomes. The Director leads the development of innovative programs, employer partnerships, and campus collaborations that integrate career readiness throughout the student experience. Through data-informed decision-making, technology integration, and a commitment to equitable access, the Director enables students to be prepared to navigate a dynamic and evolving workforce. The Director provides strategic leadership, supervision, and professional development for Career Planning staff, fostering a collaborative, high-performing team accountable for achieving student career outcomes and delivering innovative, student-centered services. Duties: Strategic Leadership & Career Outcomes - Develop and implement a comprehensive, data-informed career services strategy aligned with College’s Strategic Plan and Institutional Goals - Represent the College and collaborate with campus partners to advance institutional priorities related to student recruitment, retention, and graduation, including leveraging career outcomes and programming to support student success - Leverage career outcomes data and programming to strengthen the College’s value proposition for prospective and current students - Establish, monitor, and report student first destination career outcomes - Lead departmental program assessment efforts, including continuous improvement plans and reports, comprehensive program assessments, and other outcome measures, to evaluate program effectiveness and inform continuous improvement - Utilize data analytics and labor market insights to guide strategic priorities and resource allocation Employer & External Relations - Develop and execute a proactive employer engagement strategy to expand internships, job opportunities, and experiential learning partnerships - Cultivate and maintain relationships with local, regional, and national employers, as well as alumnae and industry partners - Collaborate with Institutional Advancement and Alumnae Relations to strengthen employer and mentoring networks - Represent the College to external stakeholders and enhance the institution’s visibility and reputation among employers Student Career Development & Readiness - Oversee the design and delivery of a comprehensive career development model that equips students with essential career readiness competencies - Ensure equitable access to high-impact practices such as internships, networking opportunities, and career counseling - Provide career counseling to students and alumnae, including administering and interpreting career assessments - Lead workshops, classroom presentations, and programming on career and professional development topics Campus Collaboration & Curriculum Integration - Partner with faculty and academic departments to integrate career development into the curriculum - Work collaboratively across campus to ensure students can effectively translate their academic, leadership, and experiential learning into clear, confident career pathways - Collaborate across campus to embed career readiness into the student experience, including first-year through senior year initiatives - Support the development of experiential learning opportunities, including internships and applied learning experiences - Serve on institutional committees related to student success, retention, and strategic planning Technology, Innovation & Operations - Oversee the implementation and optimization of career services technology platforms (e.g., career management systems - Handshake, assessment tools) - Integrate emerging technologies, including AI, to enhance career education, coaching, and operational efficiency - Ensure students are prepared to ethically and effectively use technology in the job search process - Develop and manage departmental policies, procedures, and annual budget Marketing, Outreach & Engagement - Lead a strategic communication plan to promote career services programs, resources, and outcomes - Increase student engagement and utilization of career services across all class years - Promote career success stories and outcomes to internal and external audiences Supervision & Staff Development - Supervise, mentor, and evaluate team members through regular meetings, professional development, and performance reviews - Foster a collaborative, innovative, and student-centered team culture - Train and supervise graduate student interns Access & Inclusion - Develop and implement strategies to promote equitable career outcomes for all students - Identify and address gaps in access to career opportunities and resources - Partner with campus stakeholders and employers to advance inclusive hiring practices Additional Responsibilities: - Serve as a member of Campus Committees, including the StrongPoints Advisory Committee - Maintain active participation in professional organizations and remain current on trends and best practices in career services Skills Needed: - Strategic thinking, leadership, and management skills with the ability to drive innovation and change - Strong relationship-building and collaboration skills with internal and external stakeholders - Expertise in career counseling, coaching, and student development - Ability to analyze and utilize data to inform decisions and demonstrate impact - Familiarity with career services technology platforms and emerging tools, including AI - Excellent communication, presentation, and storytelling skills - Commitment to fostering inclusive and equitable student outcomes Key Interfaces: - Interacts extensively with college administrators, faculty, and staff - Engages with students, faculty & staff, alumnae, employers, families, and community partners - Represents the College on campus and in external professional and employer communities Education, Experience, Certifications: - Master’s degree in counseling, student development, higher education administration, or a related field - Professional certifications such as career counseling/coaching credentials, assessment certifications, or leadership/HR certifications (e.g., NACE, NCDA, SHRM, Gallup Strengths Coaching) are preferred - Significant experience in career services, career development, or a related field - Demonstrated leadership experience, including supervision and program management - Experience with assessment, data analysis, and program evaluation - Proven success in building employer partnerships and external relationships preferred Working Conditions & Physical Demands: - General office setting with moderate noise - Occasional evening and weekend work, as well as travel, may be required - Valid NC Driver's License and clear driving history required. Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Please note that the search timeline for this position has been extended pending the appointment of our new Vice President for Student Affairs, who will participate in the selection process. We encourage interested candidates to continue applying and appreciate your patience as we move through this important leadership transition. Apply Now! First Name (required) 874d2cb6 Last Name (required) 02541efa Email (required) 594db1e0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 568444a7 Last Name (required) 8a6d993c Email (required) 24234982 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/head-tennis-coach-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Head Tennis Coach",
      "description": "Head Tennis Coach - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Head Tennis Coach 492537 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Meredith College, a member of the NCAA Division III and the USA South, an all-women’s college located in Raleigh, NC invites applications for the position of Head Tennis Coach. The Head Tennis Coach is responsible for providing leadership, organization, and supervision for all aspects of the tennis program, with a strong commitment to the NCAA Division III philosophy and the holistic development of student-athletes. Duties: Coaching and Player Development - Plan, implement, and oversee all training sessions, competitive strategies, and player development initiatives. - Evaluate and develop individual and team performance to achieve competitive success within the conference and at the regional/NCAA level. - Develop a positive team culture that emphasizes academic success, personal growth, well-being, and sportsmanship. Recruitment - Meet recruitment and retention goals set by the College. - Recruit student-athletes who meet Meredith College academic and athletic standards. - Provide recruitment and retention reports to the Director of Athletics. Program Administration - Oversee program operations, including scheduling, travel arrangements, equipment procurement, and facility coordination for the tennis program and tennis facility rentals. - Assist with management of the tennis budget responsibly and efficiently. - Develop and maintain a competitive schedule that allows the team to prepare and compete successfully in the conference and in post-season play. - Assist with supervision of assistant coaches, graduate assistants, and volunteers, providing direction and oversight. Compliance - Complete all necessary compliance and departmental documentation as required. - Work with the staff Compliance Officer to ensure programs and student-athletes are following all rules and regulations regarding compliance issues. Student-Athlete Support - Monitor academic progress, support retention, and graduation success. - Collaborate with academic support staff, athletic trainers, strength and conditioning coaches, and administrators to ensure the personal welfare of each student-athlete within the program. Community and Campus Engagement - Represent the tennis program at college events, alumnae functions, fundraising activities, and community outreach. - Promote the program to the public, including media, donors, and the campus community to increase visibility and revenues for the program. Secondary Duties: - Event management - Oversee outside group rentals of the tennis facility - Other duties as assigned (based on expertise) Qualifications: Required - Bachelor’s degree. - Demonstrated successful coaching experience at the collegiate or high school levels. - Knowledge and understanding of NCAA DIII philosophy, rules and regulations. - Ability to identify and recruit student-athletes. - Must be able to travel, maintain a valid driver’s license, and be trained in operating college vehicles. Valid NC Driver's License and clear driving history is required. Preferred - Master’s degree - Collegiate head coaching or high-level assistant coaching experience. - ITA membership. Working Conditions: - Ability to work non-traditional hours, including evenings, weekends, and travel for competition and recruiting. - Ability to demonstrate athletic skills and participate in on-field instruction. - Ability to move or lift items weighing up to 25-50 pounds. - Exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Application Instructions: To apply, please complete the online application. Submit a resume, cover letter, and contact information for three professional references. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Required Documents: - Resume - Cover Letter Apply Now! First Name (required) 5f43393a Last Name (required) 8e7f9d3e Email (required) e1ae4a4d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 31305d34 Last Name (required) 6df907f3 Email (required) 724150e6 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/groundskeeper-irrigation-technician-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper / Irrigation Technician",
      "description": "Groundskeeper / Irrigation Technician - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Groundskeeper / Irrigation Technician 492536 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Position is responsible for providing technical support, skills and labor towards the routine care and maintenance of a clean, beautiful and safe campus environment. Works in concert with the grounds team to maintain and enhance the function and aesthetics of the campus grounds. Position is classified as essential personnel under college policy and is subject to college and department policies regarding essential personnel. Performs essential duties as identified by management and incident response team related to inclement or hazardous weather events. Duties: - Leads in the operation, maintenance and repair of campus irrigation systems and pump stations. - Operates heavy equipment including zero turn mowers, articulating tractor, skid steer tractor, farm tractor, and large area mowers in the routine completion grounds maintenance tasks. - Routinely clears sidewalks, entrances, courtyards, campus roads and parking lots of debris using tractor with hydraulic high-powered blower. - Performs routine lawn and landscape maintenance including mowing edging, weeding, tree and shrub pruning - Routinely clears of sidewalks, entrances, courtyards, campus roads and parking lots using tractor with hydraulic high-powered blower. - Routinely collects and properly disposes of litter, trash, organic debris and recyclables in assigned areas. - Assists in the routine maintenance of athletic fields and facilities. - Assists in the repair of brick sidewalks, road signs, parking lots and campus roads surfaces. - Performs snow and storm related campus clean up, removing debris and snow from sidewalks, parking lots, and building entrances to ensure safe conditions for students, faculty and staff. - Duties may include activities related to preparation or clean-up during emergency situations. - May be required to work during campus closures. - Performs other related duties as necessary or as assigned by supervisor. Skills Needed: - Must be able to effectively communicate, verbally and in writing, with supervisor, coworkers, customers and others. - Must be highly skilled in the operation of grounds powered equipment and heavy machinery including the safe operation of: skid steer, tractor, articulating tractor, backhoe, hydraulic leaf blower reel mower, zero turn mower, snow broom and snow plow. - Must be highly skilled in the performance of grounds maintenance tasks such as mowing, edging, string-trimming, hedge-trimming, leaf and trash removal. - Must have knowledge of irrigation system repair and installation. - Must be highly skilled in the repair and maintenance of irrigation pump stations, controllers, solenoid valves and sprinkler heads. Key Interfaces: - Will work closely with Grounds Supervisor and other Grounds Staff. Education, Experience, Certifications: - High school diploma or GED preferred. - Must have irrigation repair and installation experience. - Grounds and landscape maintenance experience is required. - Valid NC Driver's License and clear driving history is required. Working conditions & physical demands: - The nature of the working environment may produce moderate levels of stress and involves discomfort and/or risk such as operating gas-powered equipment, heavy machinery and dangerous cutting equipment. - Workers are subject to environmental discomfort such as frequent exposure to loud noises, and/or extremes of heat or cold. - The work frequently requires wearing protective gear that may be uncomfortable. - Must be able to perform strenuous work that involves frequent exertion and/or periods of continuous machine operation. - Frequent lifting of objects over 50 pounds. Occasional lifting of heavy objects weighing 75 pounds or more is required. - Frequent standing and operating machinery. - May be required to work during periods of inclement weather. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 1a799bf9 Last Name (required) 6d01e8bc Email (required) af6b6be5 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 82e5e9aa Last Name (required) 9c043866 Email (required) 643f9350 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/security-officer-full-time-1st-shift-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Security Officer, Full-time 1st Shift",
      "description": "Security Officer, Full-time 1st Shift - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Security Officer, Full-time 1st Shift 492535 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Provides safety and security services to students, staff, faculty, and visitors through efficient use of departmental resources. Position is classified as essential personnel under college policy and is subject to college and department policies regarding essential personnel. Performs essential duties related to security work as identified by management during inclement weather, emergency situations, or as campus needs dictate. This position is for 1st shift, 10am - 6pm. Duties: - Responds to all calls for service and request for assistance from Meredith College student, staff, faculty and visitors. - Determines necessary and appropriate actions needed to resolve problems and answers calls for service. May need to resort to applying minimum levels of force at times. - Patrols campus by vehicle or foot. Controls access to campus and the Greenway during closing hours. - Responds to any call, fire or intrusion alarms, including suspicious person(s) and take appropriate action. - Provides traffic direction for large and small events. - Enforces parking regulations, including towing and auto-booting as appropriate. Provides car unlock, jump start, and other automotive services to students, faculty, and staff. (Flat tires can be changed if the conditions are safe) - Checks doors and window of building to ensure they are secure. Turns on and turn off interior and exterior light according to set schedules or special request. - Duties may include inclement weather safety responsibilities as necessary due to inclement weather and activities related to emergency situations. - May be required to work during campus closures. - Assist in turning on and off campus lighting for Special Events and scheduled sports activities. Qualifications: Skills Needed: - Ability to use discretion in handling difficult persons and analyze situations likely to be encountered on patrol. - Observe and retain names, faces and details of occurrences; keep detailed notes for report writing and other daily log sheets, understand and correct emergency alarm systems. - Observe legal and defensive driving practices; interpret, apply and explain rules, regulations, policies and procedures. - Ability to understand and work within the scope of authority; apply policies and procedures. Key interfaces: - Responds to calls by students, faculty, staff and visitors. - May need to confront hostile or belligerent persons in an appropriate and professional manner. Education & Experience: - High School Diploma or equivalent required. - Current NC Driver License and clear driving history required. - Previous security experience is a plus. Working conditions & physical demands: - Must be able to work any shift and respond/report for duty, as necessary. Part of duties may include general office setting with moderate noise level. Must be able to operate company vehicles. - Patrols campus outdoors and may be exposed to the weather. May be held for additional shifts during inclement weather, if relief is not possible. - Ability to navigate physical obstacles, such as walls, heights, etc. Ability to physically help students, faculty, and staff having health issues - Must be able to walk for extended distances, stand for long periods, climb stairs, and run, as necessary. - Must occasionally lift up to 50 lbs. Apply Now! First Name (required) 18883462 Last Name (required) 91ae1f4e Email (required) caeedf0a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 2b05e597 Last Name (required) 1a3d7b48 Email (required) e1a8eca9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/chair-school-of-business-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Chair",
      "description": "Chair - School of Business - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Chair - School of Business 492534 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Administrative Faculty / Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Meredith College is seeking a chair for the Business Department. Chairs at Meredith are faculty leaders responsible for overseeing academic quality, curriculum alignment, faculty performance, and operations. The Business Department offers a bachelor’s degree in business administration with concentrations in accounting, marketing, hospitality and tourism, and degrees in economics, and a minor in finance. The department also offers an MBA degree. Responsibilities: Department Curriculum - Oversee curriculum development and revisions for the department - Review and assess academic programs offered by the department - Assess general education outcomes in core courses taught within the department - Initiate new academic programs and projects when appropriate Department Operations - Manage course schedules that serve program and student needs - Manage course registrations and instructor assignments - Oversee the department's fiscal operations; develop and regularly monitor the department budget - Review and revise department information published in the college catalog - Manage the maintenance of departmental print and electronic records, including websites Personnel - Recruit, appoint, and supervise faculty in conjunction with the provost - Evaluate faculty and staff performance - Support and oversee the overall development of the department faculty and staff - Recruit, appoint, and supervise department staff and student assistants - Review faculty and staff grievances within the department Students - Recruit and retain students in the department's programs - Coordinate student advising and reviews of degree progress - Evaluate student transfer credit - Review student academic appeals and grievances Faculty Responsibilities - Teach at least two classes per semester - Participate in research and scholarly activities in the discipline - Participate and assist department faculty in college and community service activities as appropriate Required skills and experiences: - In-depth understanding of academic policies, curriculum development, and accreditation processes - Strong leadership and organizational skills, with the ability to manage budgets and personnel effectively - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills - Proven ability to support faculty research, student success initiatives, and community engagement - Demonstrated competency in data-driven decision-making Essential Job Functions: - Provide academic leadership for all programs within the department - Oversee budget development and resource allocation to support college and departmental goals and priorities - Recruit, mentor, and evaluate faculty and staff while promoting professional development - Lead efforts to assess and enhance academic programs, including accreditation and program review - Other related duties, as assigned Qualifications: An earned doctorate or terminal degree in a business; preference given to specialty area in strategic management, marketing, or economics. Required Documents: - Resume / CV - Cover Letter Apply Now! First Name (required) fe8d4883 Last Name (required) b9c60452 Email (required) f234ed46 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 02610bbf Last Name (required) 3db3bf2d Email (required) 4db62db7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/maintenance-technician-iii-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician III",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician III - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Maintenance Technician III 492526 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Maintenance Technician III is the senior technical role in the Facilities Services maintenance department. This position performs advanced maintenance, repair, installation, and preventive maintenance work across multiple trade areas with full independence, and carries significant leadership responsibility for the quality, safety, and development of the maintenance team. The Maintenance Technician III serves as the primary technical authority in the department, mentors and trains Technician I, Technician II, and Facilities Maintenance Assistant staff, and functions as lead worker in the absence of the Maintenance Supervisor. This role is the direct step up from Maintenance Technician II and the primary advancement path toward the Maintenance Supervisor role. This position is classified as essential personnel under College policy and participates in an on-call rotation for after-hours and emergency response. Duties: - Performs advanced routine, corrective, project, and preventive maintenance work across multiple trade areas — including plumbing, carpentry, painting, plastering, electrical, and machine servicing. - Diagnoses maintenance problems, determines appropriate repair approaches, and completes repairs to a high standard of workmanship. - Serves as lead worker in the absence of the Maintenance Supervisor — coordinates daily work assignments, serves as the primary point of contact for urgent work orders, and ensures work quality across the team. - Provides formal on-the-job mentorship, technical coaching, and skills development guidance to Maintenance Technician I, Technician II, and Facilities Maintenance Assistant staff. - Reviews and evaluates the quality of completed work by junior staff on shared or sequential projects; communicates quality concerns to the Maintenance Supervisor. - Contributes to the formal skills assessment of junior staff as requested by the supervisor. - Leads small renovation and repair projects from initial diagnosis through completion, including planning, material estimation, and workmanship oversight. - Estimates time and material costs of assigned projects independently; communicates material and parts needs to the inventory controller or purchasing staff. - Reads, interprets, and works from architectural drawings, engineering schematics, equipment manuals, and manufacturer documentation independently. - Participates in the hiring process for junior positions at the supervisor's request, including reviewing applications and participating in candidate interviews. - Inspects completed repairs and installations to verify proper operation, safety, workmanship, and cleanliness. - Maintains tools, equipment, vehicles, and work areas in a clean, organized, and safe condition. - Performs all work in accordance with established safety procedures, applicable codes, OSHA standards, and college policies. - Interacts professionally and courteously with students, faculty, staff, contractors, and visitors while working in occupied buildings and active campus environments. - Participates in the department's on-call rotation and responds, as assigned, to after-hours, weekend, holiday, and emergency maintenance needs. - Assists with inclement weather response, emergency response, and other campus support work as directed. - Performs other related duties as assigned. Qualifications: - High school diploma or GED required; completion of a formal trade apprenticeship or vocational program preferred. - Five or more years of progressively responsible experience in building maintenance, facilities maintenance, or related maintenance trades required, with demonstrated advanced competency across multiple trade areas. - Demonstrated experience performing advanced maintenance and repair work independently across a minimum of two trade areas. - Ability to read, interpret, and work from architectural drawings, engineering schematics, and manufacturer documentation independently. - Demonstrated ability to estimate project costs and plan multi-step repair and installation projects without supervisor input. - Demonstrated ability or willingness to mentor and develop less experienced staff. - Ability to communicate effectively in English. - Ability to work independently with minimal supervision and to coordinate the work of others as a lead worker. - Ability and willingness to participate in an on-call rotation and respond to campus as required for urgent or emergency situations. - Valid NC driver's license and acceptable driving record. - Experience using a computerized maintenance management system or work order system preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: - Advanced working knowledge of two or more building trade areas including plumbing, carpentry, painting/plastering, minor electrical, and general mechanical systems. - Ability to independently diagnose, plan, and execute complex maintenance repairs and installations across multiple trade areas. - Strong leadership, mentoring, and coaching skills; ability to coordinate the work of others and model professional standards for the team. - Working knowledge of applicable OSHA safety standards, safe work practices, and building codes relevant to maintenance trade work. - Skill in reading and working from architectural drawings, engineering schematics, and complex technical documentation. - Ability to estimate project materials and labor requirements accurately and independently. - Ability to prioritize work, manage time efficiently, and adapt to changing campus needs and daily assignments. - Ability to demonstrate dependability, professionalism, accountability, flexibility, and customer service in a service-oriented environment. - Effective written and verbal communication skills; ability to document work thoroughly and provide clear technical direction to junior staff. Physical Demands: - Ability to lift up to 50 pounds and frequently lift or carry objects weighing up to 25 pounds. - Frequent bending, reaching, climbing, walking, standing, kneeling, pushing, and pulling. - Ability to work from ladders and aerial lift equipment including boom lifts and scissor lifts as required. MEWP operator training is provided. - May be exposed to heat, cold, dust, noise, moisture, and other conditions typical of facilities maintenance work. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) bc933512 Last Name (required) f9e43532 Email (required) 3ef85b38 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) c1270771 Last Name (required) a715d971 Email (required) 1a7f4acc Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/maintenance-technician-ii-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician II",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician II - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Maintenance Technician II 492525 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. The Maintenance Technician II performs general maintenance, repair, installation, and preventive maintenance work in support of campus buildings, systems, equipment, and related spaces. This hands-on role supports residence halls, academic buildings, administrative spaces, and other campus operations and is suited for someone who is dependable, adaptable, and comfortable handling a broad range of maintenance needs. This position is classified as essential personnel under College policy and participates in an on-call rotation for after-hours and emergency response. Duties: - Performs routine, corrective, project, and preventive maintenance work as assigned. - Responds to work orders, service requests, and urgent maintenance needs in a timely, professional, and efficient manner. - Performs a variety of general building maintenance and repair tasks, including plumbing, carpentry, painting, wall and ceiling repair, hardware repairs, fixture replacement, basic electrical troubleshooting, and other general maintenance duties within skill level and training. - Troubleshoots maintenance problems and identifies repair or follow-up needs. - Inspects buildings, rooms, equipment, fixtures, and building components to identify maintenance and preventive maintenance needs. - Documents completed work, labor, materials used, and follow-up needs in the College's maintenance management system. - Maintains tools, equipment, vehicles, and work areas in a clean, organized, and safe condition. - Performs all work in accordance with established safety practices and departmental expectations. - Interacts professionally and courteously with students, faculty, staff, contractors, and visitors while working in occupied buildings and active campus environments. - Participates in the department's on-call rotation and responds, as assigned, to after-hours, weekend, holiday, and emergency maintenance needs. - Assists with inclement weather response, emergency response, and other campus support work as directed. - Performs other related duties as assigned. Qualifications: - High school diploma or equivalent preferred. - One to two years of hands-on experience in building maintenance, facilities, property maintenance, construction, or a closely related trade required. Candidates with apartment, hotel, commercial, or institutional maintenance experience are encouraged to apply. - Experience performing a broad range of general maintenance and repair work in occupied facilities preferred. - Demonstrated experience in one or more of the following trade areas: general building maintenance and repair; basic plumbing; carpentry; painting and wall repair; basic electrical; or general mechanical/equipment repair. - Ability to read and follow work orders, equipment manuals, diagrams, labels, and written instructions. - Ability to communicate effectively in English. - Ability to work independently with limited supervision and also function effectively as part of a team. - Ability and willingness to participate in an on-call rotation and respond to campus as required for urgent or emergency situations. - Valid NC driver's license and acceptable driving record. - Experience using a computerized maintenance management system or work order system preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: - Working knowledge of tools, materials, methods, and safety practices used in general building maintenance. - Ability to perform a broad range of maintenance and repair work within skill level and training. - Ability to troubleshoot common building-related problems and complete repairs safely and effectively. - Ability to prioritize work, manage time efficiently, and adapt to changing campus needs and daily assignments. - Ability to demonstrate dependability, professionalism, flexibility, and customer service in a service-oriented environment. - Ability to work effectively in occupied buildings and maintain productive working relationships with others in a campus setting. Physical Demands: - Ability to lift up to 50 pounds and frequently lift or carry objects weighing up to 25 pounds. - Frequent bending, reaching, climbing, walking, standing, kneeling, pushing, and pulling. - Ability to work from ladders and aerial lift equipment including boom lifts and scissor lifts as required. MEWP operator training is provided. - May be exposed to heat, cold, dust, noise, moisture, and other conditions typical of facilities maintenance work. Required Documents: - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) 57e6c058 Last Name (required) 3650d279 Email (required) 84f24814 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 68b3255d Last Name (required) 3935ceb2 Email (required) 9b73f03f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/police-officer-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "Police Officer - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Police Officer 492519 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. Provides comprehensive law enforcement, safety, and security services to students, faculty, staff, and visitors through the efficient use of departmental resources. Enforces applicable federal laws, North Carolina General Statutes, and Meredith College policies. This position is classified as essential personnel under College policy and is subject to requirements regarding essential personnel. Performs essential police duties during inclement weather, emergency situations, or as campus needs dictate. This role also supports a developing campus police department by contributing to the continuous improvement of operations, procedures, and service delivery, while helping to foster a culture of professionalism, accountability, and community engagement. Duties: - Responds to all calls for service and requests for assistance from Meredith College students, faculty, staff, and visitors - Exercises independent judgment to determine appropriate actions to resolve incidents, including detention, search, arrest, issuance of citations, and criminal charge filing in accordance with North Carolina law - Applies only the minimum level of force necessary, consistent with training, law, and departmental policy - Patrols campus by vehicle and on foot; operates a law enforcement patrol vehicle during day and night shifts - Controls access to campus facilities and designated areas, including the Greenway, during established hours - Responds to calls, fire alarms, and intrusion alarms, including suspicious persons, and takes appropriate enforcement or protective action - Conducts preliminary and follow-up investigations by interviewing victims, witnesses, suspects, and confidential informants; collects, preserves, and documents physical and digital evidence - Prepares detailed written reports, case files, and documentation in accordance with departmental policy and legal standards - Provides testimony in criminal, traffic, and judicial proceedings as required - Provides traffic, parking, and crowd control for campus events and special functions - Conducts safety and security inspections of campus facilities, including checking doors, windows, and lighting - Renders emergency and non-emergency medical assistance, including First Aid, CPR, and AED use, until relieved by medical professionals - Participates in community-oriented policing, crime prevention initiatives, campus outreach, and educational programming - Builds positive relationships with students, faculty, and staff through visibility, engagement, and service - May perform administrative duties such as campus bank deposits or other assignments as directed - Performs duties related to emergency response, disaster operations, and inclement weather safety responsibilities - Participates in the development and refinement of departmental practices, procedures, and service delivery models - Provides feedback to supervisors to support the growth and continuous improvement of a developing department Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: - Knowledge of federal laws, North Carolina General Statutes, and College policies applicable to sworn law enforcement officers - Ability to analyze complex situations, exercise sound judgment, and use discretion when dealing with difficult or hostile individuals - Ability to observe and recall names, faces, and details; maintain accurate notes and reports - Skill in operating law enforcement equipment, including radios, vehicles, and defensive tools - Ability to communicate clearly and professionally with diverse populations - Ability to understand and work within the scope of authority while applying policies and procedures consistently - Ability to adapt to evolving policies, procedures, and operational needs in a developing department - Commitment to maintaining the highest standards of integrity, professionalism, and ethical conduct Education & Experience: - High School Diploma or equivalent required - Current North Carolina Driver License with a clear driving history - Current certification as a sworn Law Enforcement Officer by the State of North Carolina (BLET), or ability to obtain certification within eight (8) months of hire Training & Certification Requirements: - Successful completion of required in-service training and annual firearms qualification - Certification or ability to obtain certification in ASP baton, chemical agents, First Aid, CPR, and AED - Compliance with North Carolina Criminal Justice Education and Training Standards Commission requirements - Successful completion of a basic physical fitness assessment prior to appointment and/or during probationary period, consistent with departmental standards Working conditions & physical demands: - Ability to work modified 3rd shift (6 p.m. – 2 a.m.), rotating shifts, including nights, weekends, holidays, and emergency call-back - Duties performed in office, vehicle, and outdoor environments; subject to varying weather conditions - May be required to remain on duty during inclement weather or emergencies when relief is unavailable - Medium work: ability to walk extended distances, stand for long periods, climb stairs, run as necessary, and lift up to 50 pounds - Ability to navigate physical obstacles and assist individuals experiencing medical or safety emergencies - Vision correctable to meet North Carolina law enforcement standards, including color vision requirements Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume Apply Now! First Name (required) edb4e443 Last Name (required) 4e64da5e Email (required) 4bdc64f9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) f9b92bc8 Last Name (required) 7561d46a Email (required) 8f8fc3fa Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://meredith.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-director-of-financial-assistance-raleigh-nc-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Financial Assistance",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Financial Assistance - Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Home Contact Us Working at Meredith Applying for a Position Nondiscrimination Statement Americans with Disabilities Immigration Information Employee Benefits Payroll Information About Meredith About Meredith Getting to Meredith See all jobs My Settings Kiosk mode Assistant Director of Financial Assistance 492517 Raleigh, NC, North Carolina, United States Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Notice: If you are seeing this position posted on a job board other than the official Meredith College career posting page, please know that any pay range included is not authorized or approved by Meredith College and may not reflect the actual pay rate for the position. General Purpose of Position Assists in administering need-based and non-need-based federal, state, private, and institutional financial assistance programs and ensures compliance with all federal, state, and institutional policies. Essential Duties & Responsibilities: -Manage and work with Institutional Advancement, regarding the underwriting of Institutional Endowed scholarships and awards -Monitor students regarding their satisfactory academic progress in federal aid programs -Monitor students to ensure student recipients remain in good standing regarding their specific institutional scholarship fund. -Counsel, verify, package, and award both prospective and upper class students -Serve as primary FA Counselor for those studying abroad -Performs other duties as assigned Skills Needed: -Experience working with Microsoft Office, including Microsoft Word, PowerPoint, Excel and the ability to work with mainframe database systems. -Experienced in providing customer service -Proficient written and oral communications skills -Excellent interpersonal skills Key interfaces: -Interaction with continuing students, prospective students, faculty, and staff of the college -Interaction with Federal and State officials -Interaction with student loan agencies Education & Experience: -Bachelor’s Degree required, master degree preferred -At least three years experience in financial assistance and/or significant work experience. Working conditions & physical demands -General office setting with moderate noise level Required Documents: - Cover Letter - Resume/CV Apply Now! First Name (required) d8e41259 Last Name (required) 1b982cc4 Email (required) 0175c9c2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Contact Information 1st Floor Park Center (919) 760-8898 Fax: (919) 760-8164 hr@meredith.edu Apply Now First Name (required) 7462d32b Last Name (required) d548cba3 Email (required) b373bf09 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me What Makes Us Strong Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Useful links A-Z Meredith College Diversity Statement Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Family Community Career Planning: Employers En Español What Makes Us Strong 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298 | (919) 760-8600 Fax: (919) 760-8330 1-800-MEREDITH | © 2022 All Rights Reserved. Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://www.meredith.edu/employers-career-planning/": {
      "title": "Career Planning: Employers",
      "description": "Career Planning: Employers - Meredith College Skip to content Navigation A-Z Careers Quick Links Accessibility Apply Arts Events Brightspace Calendar Campus Services Library MyMeredith News People Self Service Visit Information For Prospective Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Families Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Giving Support Give now A-Z Careers Quick Links Accessibility Apply Arts Events Brightspace Calendar Campus Services Library MyMeredith News People Self Service Visit Information For Prospective Students Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Families Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Giving Support Give now Search Search Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student life Athletics About STRONGPOINTS® Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student life Athletics About STRONGPOINTS® Career Planning: Employers Engage with Meredith Students Post a Position FAQs Hiring International Students Employer Recruiting Opportunities Internships Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Staff Meredith College welcomes the opportunity to work with you and your organization as you seek students, recent graduates and experienced alumnae for internships, co-ops, and full-time career opportunities. Please contact Mackenzie Bradley, Career Planning Program Coordinator, at mrbradley@meredith.edu to learn more about upcoming opportunities to meet Meredith students and how to build a recruiting partnership. Find Meredith students on Handshake! The Office of Career Planning is excited to welcome you to Handshake, a one-stop platform to manage all of your on- and off-campus recruiting needs, share and update job postings, connect with students, and more. All organizations recruiting at Meredith College must adhere to the Meredith College Recruiting Guidelines . Please note: employers and positions are vetted by our team before being posted. Helpful Handshake Resources: Register for an Employer Account Connect with Meredith College Approve Staff Members Questions? Contact support@joinhandshake.com Interested in hiring a part-time tutor, teacher, or nanny? The Office of Financial Assistance hosts a job board for part-time positions. Please complete and return their employment form to finaid@meredith.edu . Office of Career Planning Contact Information Mackenzie Bradley Career Planning Program Coordinator 205 Park Center (919) 760-8343 mrbradley@meredith.edu Facebook Tiktok Instagram Youtube X-twitter Threads Linkedin Giphy Logo Book an event! ONE OF AMERICA'S BEST COLLEGES PRINCETON REVIEW U.S. NEWS NICHE What Makes Us Strong A-Z Careers Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Accessibility at Meredith Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy A-Z Careers Giving at Meredith Emergency Planning Accessibility at Meredith Contact Us Title IX Information Accreditation & Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Families Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Families Community Career Planning: Employers En Español (919)760-8600 (919)760-8330 3800 Hillsborough Street Raleigh, NC 27607-5298  © 2026 All Rights Reserved Apply Today Give Now Quick Links A-Z Apply to Meredith Arts Events Brightspace Calendar Campus Services Careers MyMeredith News People Self Service A-Z Apply to Meredith Arts Events Brightspace Calendar Campus Services Careers MyMeredith News People Self Service Primary Navigation Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student life Athletics About STRONGPOINTS® Academics Admissions Financial Aid Student life Athletics About STRONGPOINTS® Information For Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Families Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Prospective Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumnae Parents & Families Community Career Planning: Employers En Español Giving Ways to Give Annual giving Faculty & Staff Gifts Giving Societies Give now Ways to Give Annual giving Faculty & Staff Gifts Giving Societies Give now"
